#: dcrawsettingswidget.cpp:98
msgid "RAW Decoding Settings (dcraw %1)"
msgstr ""

#: dcrawsettingswidget.cpp:106
msgid "Interpolate RGB as four colors"
msgstr ""

#: dcrawsettingswidget.cpp:107
msgid ""
"<p><b>Interpolate RGB as four colors</b>"
"<p>The default is to assume that all green pixels are the same. If even-row "
"green pixels are more sensitive to ultraviolet light than odd-row this "
"difference causes a mesh pattern in the output; using this option solves this "
"problem with minimal loss of detail."
"<p>To resume, this option blurs the image a little, but it eliminates false 2x2 "
"mesh patterns with VNG quality method or mazes with AHD quality method."
msgstr ""

#: dcrawsettingswidget.cpp:121
msgid "Use camera white balance"
msgstr ""

#: dcrawsettingswidget.cpp:122
msgid ""
"<p><b>Use camera white balance</b>"
"<p>Use the camera's custom white-balance settings. The default is to use fixed "
"daylight values, calculated from sample images. If this can't be found, reverts "
"to the default."
msgstr ""

#: dcrawsettingswidget.cpp:131
msgid "Automatic color balance"
msgstr ""

#: dcrawsettingswidget.cpp:132
msgid ""
"<p><b>Automatic color balance</b>"
"<p>The default is to use a fixed color balance based on a white card "
"photographed in sunlight."
"<p>"
msgstr ""

#: dcrawsettingswidget.cpp:140
msgid "Use Super-CCD secondary sensors"
msgstr ""

#: dcrawsettingswidget.cpp:141
msgid ""
"<p><b>Use Super CCD secondary sensors</b>"
"<p>For Fuji Super CCD SR cameras, use the secondary sensors, in effect "
"underexposing the image by four stops to reveal detail in the highlights. For "
"all other camera types this option is ignored."
"<p>"
msgstr ""

#: dcrawsettingswidget.cpp:151
msgid "Highlights:"
msgstr ""

#: dcrawsettingswidget.cpp:153
msgid "Solid white"
msgstr ""

#: dcrawsettingswidget.cpp:154
msgid "Unclip"
msgstr ""

#: dcrawsettingswidget.cpp:155
msgid "Reconstruct"
msgstr ""

#: dcrawsettingswidget.cpp:156
msgid ""
"<p><b>Highlights</b>"
"<p>Select here the highlight cliping method:"
"<p><b>Solid white</b>: clip all highlights to solid white"
"<p><b>Unclip</b>: leave highlights unclipped in various shades of pink"
"<p><b>Reconstruct</b>: reconstruct highlights using a level value."
msgstr ""

#: dcrawsettingswidget.cpp:166
msgid "Level:"
msgstr ""

#: dcrawsettingswidget.cpp:169
msgid ""
"<p><b>Level</b>"
"<p>Specify the reconstruct highlights level of ouput image. Low value favor "
"whites and high value favor colors."
msgstr ""

#: dcrawsettingswidget.cpp:177
msgid "Brightness:"
msgstr "Disgleirdeb:"

#: dcrawsettingswidget.cpp:181
msgid ""
"<p><b>Brighness</b>"
"<p>Specify the brightness level of ouput image.The default value is 1.0."
"<p>"
msgstr ""

#: dcrawsettingswidget.cpp:189
msgid "Quality:"
msgstr ""

#: dcrawsettingswidget.cpp:191
msgid "Bilinear interpolation"
msgstr ""

#: dcrawsettingswidget.cpp:192
msgid "VNG interpolation"
msgstr ""

#: dcrawsettingswidget.cpp:193
msgid "AHD interpolation"
msgstr ""

#: dcrawsettingswidget.cpp:194
msgid ""
"<p><b>Quality</b>"
"<p>Select here the demosaicing RAW images decoding interpolation method. A "
"demosaicing algorithm is a digital image process used to interpolate a complete "
"image from the partial raw data received from the color-filtered image sensor "
"internal to many digital cameras in form of a matrix of colored pixels. Also "
"known as CFA interpolation or color reconstruction, another common spelling is "
"demosaicing. There are 3 methods to demosaicing RAW images:"
"<p><b>Bilinear</b>: use high-speed but low-quality bilinear interpolation "
"(default - for slow computer). In this method, the red value of a non-red pixel "
"is computed as the average of the adjacent red pixels, and similar for blue and "
"green."
"<p><b>VNG</b>: use Variable Number of Gradients interpolation. This method "
"computes gradients near the pixel of interest and uses the lower gradients "
"(representing smoother and more similar parts of the image) to make an "
"estimate."
"<p><b>AHD</b>: use Adaptive Homogeneity-Directed interpolation. This method "
"selects the direction of interpolation so as to maximize a homogeneity metric, "
"thus typically minimizing color artifacts."
"<p>"
msgstr ""

#: dcrawsettingswidget.cpp:217
msgid "Enable noise reduction"
msgstr ""

#: dcrawsettingswidget.cpp:218
msgid ""
"<p><b>Enable Noise Reduction</b>"
"<p>Toggle bilateral filter to smooth noise while preserving edges. This option "
"can be use to reduce low noise. The pictures edges are preserved because it is "
"applied in CIELab color space instead of RGB."
"<p>"
msgstr ""

#: dcrawsettingswidget.cpp:228
msgid "Domain:"
msgstr ""

#: dcrawsettingswidget.cpp:229
msgid ""
"<p><b>Domain</b>"
"<p>Set here the noise reduction Sigma Domain in units of pixels. The default "
"value is 2.0."
"<p>"
msgstr ""

#: dcrawsettingswidget.cpp:239
msgid "Range:"
msgstr ""

#: dcrawsettingswidget.cpp:240
msgid ""
"<p><b>Range</b>"
"<p>Set here the noise reduction Sigma Range in units of CIELab colorspace. The "
"default value is 4.0."
"<p>"
msgstr ""

#: dcrawsettingswidget.cpp:248
msgid "Color space:"
msgstr ""

#: dcrawsettingswidget.cpp:250
msgid "Raw (linear)"
msgstr ""

#: dcrawsettingswidget.cpp:251
msgid "sRGB"
msgstr ""

#: dcrawsettingswidget.cpp:252
msgid "Adobe RGB"
msgstr ""

#: dcrawsettingswidget.cpp:253
msgid "Wide Gamut"
msgstr ""

#: dcrawsettingswidget.cpp:254
msgid "Pro-Photo"
msgstr ""

#: dcrawsettingswidget.cpp:255
msgid ""
"<p><b>Color space</b>"
"<p>Select here the output color space used to decode RAW data."
"<p><b>Raw (linear)</b>: in this mode, none output color space is used during "
"RAW decoding."
"<p><b>sRGB</b>: this color space is an RGB color space, created cooperatively "
"by Hewlett-Packard and Microsoft, that is the best choice for images destined "
"for the Web and portrait photography."
"<p><b>Adobe RGB</b>: this color space is an RGB color space, developed by "
"Adobe, that used for photography applications such as advertising and fine art."
"<p><b>Wide Gamut</b>: this color space is is an expanded version of the Adobe "
"RGB color space."
"<p><b>Pro-Photo</b>: this color space is an RGB color space, developed by "
"Kodak, that offers an especially large gamut designed for use with photographic "
"output in mind."
msgstr ""

